jei.immersivenuclear.precipitation_unit.info=5x7x5 multiblock (92 blocks, of them 4 Chemical Engineering Blocks and 6 Radioactive Handling Blocks). Build the structure and hit the redstone engineering block (front side) with the Engineer's Hammer. Purified solution in at the tank end (left), precipitating agent in at the back; chemical effluent out at the front, at the foot of the screw; wet concentrate out at the screw end; energy on the heavy engineering blocks of the screw end corner. Each batch (provisional): the full tank, 12000 mB of solution, and 6 agents give 24 wet concentrate and 9000 mB of effluent. A redstone signal stops the machine (the hammer inverts that).
