ie.manual.entry.in_precipitation_unit.subtext=From liquid to solid
ie.manual.entry.in_precipitation_unit0=The Precipitation Unit turns the uranium dissolved in the purified solution into a solid and separates it from the liquid. The structure is built as shown above and formed by using the Engineer's Hammer on the redstone engineering block at the front.
ie.manual.entry.in_precipitation_unit1=Each batch is the full agitated tank: 12000 mB of purified solution. Once it is full, 6 precipitating agents are dosed and the agitator mixes for 60 seconds; then the slurry drops from the conical bottom into the screw, which lifts the solid up to the chute while the liquid runs back down. 24 wet uranium concentrate and 9000 mB of chemical effluent per batch.
ie.manual.entry.in_precipitation_unit2=The solution goes in at the tank end (left, seen from the front), the agent at the back. The chemical effluent comes out at the front, at the foot of the screw, and the concentrate at the far end of the screw. Energy goes into the heavy engineering blocks of the corner by the screw's head.
ie.manual.entry.in_precipitation_unit3=The precipitating agent.
tile.immersivenuclear.industrial_dryer.name=Industrial Dryer
item.immersivenuclear.industrial_dryer.name=Industrial Dryer
jei.immersivenuclear.industrial_dryer.info=5x7x4 multiblock (86 blocks, of them 2 Radioactive Handling Blocks). Build the structure and hit the redstone engineering block (front side) with the Engineer's Hammer. Wet uranium concentrate in through the feed hopper on top of the chamber; empty Concentrate Drums in at the back of the north end, onto the drum station's conveyor; yellowcake and full drums out at the discharge end, under the chamber; process condensate out at the back, by the condensate tank; energy on the heavy engineering blocks of the drive end. Each batch (provisional, 90 s, 76800 IF): 24 wet concentrate give 16 yellowcake and 2000 mB of process condensate. A redstone signal stops the machine (the hammer inverts that).
jei.immersivenuclear.sulfuric_acid_unit.info=5x7x8 multiblock (125 blocks, of them 5 Chemical Engineering Blocks). Build the structure and hit the redstone engineering block (front side) with the Engineer's Hammer. Sulfur (dust or block, from any mod) in through the hopper on the burner; water in at the top of the absorption tower; sulfuric acid out under the pump tank; steam out at the back; energy on the heavy engineering blocks at the back. Each cycle (provisional, 5 s, 3200 IF): 1 sulfur and 500 mB of water give 500 mB of sulfuric acid and 250 mB of steam; a block of sulfur is nine cycles in one. With its tank full the steam is vented through the relief valve. A redstone signal stops the machine (the hammer inverts that).
jei.immersivenuclear.steam.info=Steam, a by-product of the Sulfuric Acid Unit (its waste heat boiler). Other mods' machines that run on steam can take it. Hot: it scalds.
