ie.manual.entry.in_industrial_dryer.name=Industrial Dryer
ie.manual.entry.in_industrial_dryer.subtext=The last of the water
ie.manual.entry.in_industrial_dryer0=The Industrial Dryer drives the water out of the wet uranium concentrate and leaves yellowcake, the end of the first line. The structure is built as shown above and formed by using the Engineer's Hammer on the redstone engineering block at the front.
ie.manual.entry.in_industrial_dryer1=Each batch takes 24 wet uranium concentrate, what the Precipitation Unit gives in one batch, and lasts 90 seconds: loading, heating, 60 seconds of drying while the paddles turn the concentrate over, then cooling and discharge. 16 yellowcake and 2000 mB of process condensate per batch. A scrubber on the vapour line catches the fines the vapour carries off: every 4 batches they come back as one more yellowcake. A batch only starts with room for its whole output. The process condensate goes back to the Chemical Processing Unit as recycled liquor.
ie.manual.entry.in_industrial_dryer2=The wet concentrate goes in through the feed hopper on top of the chamber. The yellowcake comes out at the discharge end, under the chamber, and the process condensate at the back, by the condensate tank. Energy goes into the heavy engineering blocks by the drive.
ie.manual.entry.in_industrial_dryer3=Beside the chamber runs the drum loading station. Concentrate Drums go in at the back of the north end, empty (up to a stack) or partly filled (one at a time): the conveyor brings each one under the spout, where the yellowcake pours into it, and once it holds 64 it goes on, sealed, and out with the yellowcake. While drums are at the station the yellowcake goes into them; without drums it comes out loose, as before.
ie.manual.entry.in_industrial_dryer4=The Concentrate Drum: one slot of yellowcake, up to 64. Broken, it keeps its yellowcake inside.
