ie.manual.entry.in_sulfuric_acid_unit.subtext=The contact process
ie.manual.entry.in_sulfuric_acid_unit0=The Sulfuric Acid Unit makes sulfuric acid from sulfur and water, for the enrichment line. The structure is built as shown above; hit the redstone engineering block (front side) with the Engineer's Hammer to form it.
ie.manual.entry.in_sulfuric_acid_unit1=The sulfur burns in the air from the blower, the boiler cools the gas (and makes steam), the converter's catalyst beds turn it into sulfur trioxide and the absorption tower turns that into sulfuric acid. Each 5 s cycle takes 1 sulfur (dust, from any mod) and 500 mB of water and gives 500 mB of sulfuric acid and 250 mB of steam, drawing 32 IF/t. A block of sulfur makes one cycle nine times as long, with nine times the water and the output. Sulfur goes in through the hopper on the burner and water at the top of the tower; the acid comes out under the pump tank and the steam at the back (with its tank full the steam is vented). A redstone signal stops it (the hammer inverts that).
