ie.manual.entry.in_hf_kiln.subtext=Fluorite and sulfuric acid
ie.manual.entry.in_hf_kiln0=The Hydrofluoric Acid Kiln makes hydrofluoric acid from fluorite and sulfuric acid, for the Conversion Unit. The structure is built as shown above; hit the redstone engineering block (front side) with the Engineer's Hammer to form it.
ie.manual.entry.in_hf_kiln1=A rotary kiln: the fluorite dust and the sulfuric acid go into the feed head and react in the heated, turning drum; the hydrofluoric acid leaves as a gas through the scrubber and the condenser into its tank, the gypsum leaves at the discharge head. Each 10 s cycle takes 1 fluorite dust and 500 mB of sulfuric acid and gives 500 mB of hydrofluoric acid and 1 gypsum, drawing 64 IF/t. Fluorite goes in on top of the feed head and the acid at its foot (north end); the gypsum and the hydrofluoric acid come out at the south end. A redstone signal stops it (the hammer inverts that).
