jei.immersivenuclear.hf_kiln.info=5x7x3 multiblock (86 blocks, of them 5 Chemical Engineering Blocks). Build the structure and hit the redstone engineering block (front side) with the Engineer's Hammer. Fluorite dust (from any mod) in on top of the feed head; sulfuric acid in at the feed head's foot (north end); gypsum and hydrofluoric acid out at the south end; energy on the heavy engineering blocks at the back. Each cycle (provisional, 10 s, 12800 IF): 1 fluorite dust and 500 mB of sulfuric acid give 500 mB of hydrofluoric acid and 1 gypsum. A redstone signal stops the machine (the hammer inverts that).
