jei.immersivenuclear.fluorination_ash.info=What stays at the bottom of the Conversion Unit's fluorination reactor: the fluorides of the impurities the yellowcake still carried and a little uranium that did not react. It comes out now and then. Goes back to the Chemical Processing Unit, in place of the ore, to recover its uranium (the Conversion Unit is still to come).
jei.immersivenuclear.depleted_uranium_oxide.info=A stable, dark powder: the uranium left after the enrichment took the uranium-235 away, made safe to store by the Deconversion. In IE's Arc Furnace with coke dust it becomes Depleted Uranium Ingots.
jei.immersivenuclear.depleted_uranium_ingot.info=Depleted uranium: barely radioactive and very dense, about 1.7 times as heavy as lead. For radiation shielding better than lead's, heavy machine parts and, later, fertile material for a reactor (still to come).
